Negative control for a fence being READABLE (`AC3.3`/`AC3.4` · `R6-11`).

Leaves `Markdown`'s own prose code-block theme in place: a dark `pre` whose text
colour is that same dark. The content is all there in the DOM and the browser
paints a solid slab — which is why the operator kept reporting the Code and
Scenario sheets as EMPTY while every registration spec was green.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the fence-block spec — the block hands the `pre` and its `code` back to the
pane's own surface and colour.

